From c91e24ec6d5d4cd0ddf5b9315ab3e26c49c2668f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 10:46:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 49/50] PhoenixInverterSerial: add Phoenixtec RS-232 solar
 inverter plugin

Talks to AEG Protect PV 2800 (and OEM siblings: CMS2000, SunEzy, Orion,
Eaton, KLNE SunTeams) over RS-232 9600 8N1 using the Phoenixtec binary
framing protocol documented in aeg-inverter/PROTOCOL.md.

HTYPE_PhoenixInverterSerial = 130. The hardware name contains 'USB' so
Hardware.js shows the serial-port selector div automatically -- both
direct RS-232 and USB-serial adapters are valid deployment paths.

State machine: Disconnected -> Init -> SerialQuery -> SerialConfirm ->
Version -> ParamFmt -> Params -> DataFmt -> Polling. Full startup
handshake required before polling; timeout in any step triggers
reconnect with 30s backoff.

Devices created (NodeIDs stable):
  1  kWh meter   PAC (W) + ETOTAL (kWh)
  2  Voltage     VPV -- DC panel voltage
  3  Voltage     VAC -- AC grid voltage
  4  Current     IAC -- AC grid current
  5  Custom      FAC -- grid frequency (Hz)
  6  Temperature TEMP -- inverter heat-sink
  7  Custom      ETODAY -- energy today (kWh)
  8  Alert       operating mode + fault register summary
  9  Text        model / firmware / serial (set once at startup)

Protocol notes:
- Frame: AA AA | src(2) | dst(2) | opcode(2) | len(1) | payload | csum(2)
- Checksum = sum of all frame bytes mod 65536, big-endian
- Pre-confirm dst=0x0000; post-confirm dst=0x0001
- datafmt and data payloads carry no leading count byte -- LEN from the
  frame header is authoritative
- ETOTAL = ETOTALH*256 + ETOTALL*0.1 kWh; published even when PAC=0
- ZAC=0xFFFF is a sentinel (not measured), not published
- ETODAY zeroed before 09:00 when >1 kWh (stale from previous day)
- Serial string sourced from serial-query response, not version payload

Thread model: readCallback (ASyncSerial I/O thread) only writes to the
ring buffer; ParseIncomingData and all state-machine logic run on the
worker thread, avoiding data races on shared state.

Signed-off-by: Koen Kooi <koen@dominion.thruhere.net>
